      what this project does.
    - The module's "DistributionLicense: GPL" field is metadata describing the
      SWORD module package, which this project does not redistribute: the build
      extracts the text with mod2imp and ships a derived database.
    - The Crown's rights in the base text are territorial. Perpetual Crown
      copyright applies in the United Kingdom, and CrossWire records that in most
      of the world the Authorized Version has passed out of copyright and is
      freely reproduced.

  The obligations a GPL reading would impose are met regardless, because they cost
  nothing: attribution and copyright notices are preserved here and in the
  application's attribution UI; the licence text is included at
  LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt (the module records "GPL" with no version, and SWORD itself
  is GPL-2.0); and scripts/fetch-kjv.sh is the corresponding source, checksum-pinned
  to the exact upstream archive and to the exact mod2imp output.

  Copyleft is not treated as reaching this project's MIT-licensed code:
  content.sqlite is data the application reads, not code linked into it.


